<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/VARRO/de_re_rustica/e/4/text/265>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 265 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/VARRO/de_re_rustica/e/4> ;
      zoo:text "17 Storr-Best refers to Aulus Gellius, III.9, where the story is told of a 'certain Seius' who possessed a very beauti­ful horse, which, however, brought disaster to its successive owners, so that it became proverbial to say of an unlucky man, 'He has a Seian horse'; and suggests a play on the proverb." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/VARRO/de_re_rustica/e/4/text/156>
